  "description": "An elite algorithmic problem-solving CP contest , designed to test analytical limits, data structure mastery, and computational complexity optimization under strict time constraints. Participants tackle multi-tiered problems ranging from dynamic programming to graph theory on standard ICPC scoring. Rules: Participants can be from any recognized university or college. Participants must connect to the contest server; plagiarism and AI-assisted code generation will lead to immediate disqualification. Standard ICPC-style rules apply: ranking is determined by total solved problems and penalty time . Languages permitted: C++, C, Java, and Python 3 . Finalists must carry valid student ID cards for onsite verification. Registration must be done on Unstop and the form (both compulsory before the Prelims) - https://forms.gle/EfffoSn5Nfj4hj2j9 Format: Round 1: Online Preliminary Qualifier A 1 hour algorithmic coding challenge hosted on the live contest platform . Top 75 will advance to the on-campus Grand Finale . Round 2: On-Campus Grand Finale A high-intensity 2 -hour onsite showdown with hidden evaluation test cases. Scoreboard will be frozen during the final 60 minutes to heighten suspense. Participants must bring their own laptops",
